class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1536 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1539 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1540 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1541 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1603 14 "// the type attribute cache: an MRO set"] [1612 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1613 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1621 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1622 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1636 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1639 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [1640 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [1641 1 "// makes lists"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[122 29] [140 37] [177 37] [190 67] [201 63] [206 68] [211 67] [227 37] [244 37] [266 37] [302 37] [306 25] [320 38] [325 37] [335 37] [382 38] [387 37] [405 26] [419 29] [446 25] [448 38] [466 37] [490 25] [492 24] [507 24] [563 26] [573 23] [616 34] [619 36] [627 54] [650 55] [689 49] [705 32] [712 50] [766 21] [767 36] [778 43] [831 38] [839 28] [841 56] [881 42] [907 50] [917 53] [922 48] [923 26] [938 31] [939 32] [948 30] [955 31] [991 43] [1030 51] [1037 29] [1043 36] [1071 21] [1077 21] [1090 38] [1105 23] [1106 36] [1118 25] [1140 76] [1179 71] [1218 39] [1229 23] [1241 34] [1262 25] [1278 43] [1288 47] [1295 61] [1306 25] [1350 28] 